{"title":"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>(<i>Kiran Kedlaya</i>) Three nonnegative real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae5f496b8ddda88b5cbbc06ccb02bee0580fd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> are written on a blackboard. These numbers have the property that there exist integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, not all zero, satisfying <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/b/bbb0482ea61ac98361f0a173e290076f4df71757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1r_1 + a_2r_2 + a_3r_3 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" />. We are permitted to perform the following operation: find two numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> on the blackboard with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854f2adcb15b6f0a4235bc1e66f1a18f60a9be1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\le y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"46\" height=\"17\" />, then erase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/d/e3d2d36ed8ae2ac20e4bcec402980a11639c40c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y - x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" /> in its place. Prove that after a finite number of such operations, we can end up with at least one <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the blackboard.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Every time we perform an operation on the numbers on the blackboard <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/565730eb5641d767b8cffb532b96620c0f5d2845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R = \\left &lt; r_1, r_2, r_3 \\right &gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"114\" height=\"19\" />, we perform the corresponding operation on the integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39add0f03714c32b948a979976eeb65ac4bdc355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\left &lt; a_1, a_2, a_3 \\right &gt;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"19\" /> so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/c/80cee013ee2848986a21cd895ecc02f58b3868d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R \\cdot A = 0$\" width=\"73\" height=\"13\" /> continues to hold.  (For example, if we replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/6/db60cd6cd7b73d51f6dc0ca040d698811cfba6c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1 - r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"10\" /> then we replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/f/67f67347b4a28ef5ee9c25b7736d246f2560f471.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />.)\n</p><p>It's possible to show we can always pick an operation so that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/8/608d3b14cc7d93427f106e288195769d7c476fa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"19\" /> is strictly decreasing. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a>, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/0/58059771e72d79bb50d2fe040ad4b891ad98a6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3 &gt; r_2 &gt; r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"93\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> be positive. Then it cannot be true that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/7/3e7b9924603cea7baaca27e1d8a40a88e39ff992.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac { - a_3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"33\" height=\"33\" />, or else <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757a64e84d5eed567e03153a0086df29b1739df9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1r_1 + a_2r_2 + a_3r_3 &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"175\" height=\"15\" />. Without loss of generality, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16ef37d46cfecadc189d80775f5780dab3d853d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 &lt; \\frac { - a_3}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"33\" />. Then we can replace <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/7/99721381691445ba7f546e558f4f9a0201a0c74b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1 + a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/e/5ae5f496b8ddda88b5cbbc06ccb02bee0580fd0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/d/92d66602e7fdbaaf87ef17d10796ae9be500e50f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_3 - r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"10\" /> to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7ded470c5c84305a67acacfe0ff329cf6c4597be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|A|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> smaller. Since it is a strictly decreasing sequence of positive integers, after a finite number of operations we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/8/7b884e7353eb10cf92f673224bf427b4c2ea52e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"15\" />. We can now  see that this result holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/1/0e145c3c9b6671e0cf080f428b4e4dcadaeab409.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(r_1,r_2,0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> if and only if it holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/b/c3b2fac1c18e39dca66d3c42dc8fb5b4cb8c9018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1,\\frac{r_2}{r_1},0)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"66\" height=\"35\" />. We can see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/2/f0264e047b5b8e1a8f4c0ec13e29223ee217c3af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{r_2}{r_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"18\" height=\"35\" /> is a rational number given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> = 0. It is a well known result of the euclidean algorithm that if we continue to perform these operations, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/c/adc143c3f887fa7e92fd80d91bb22af51b4abd77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/4/0b4f3f4b698ce35667432041e168f7653533fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> will eventually be 0.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>&lt;url&gt;viewtopic.php?t=202910 Discussion on AoPS/MathLinks&lt;/url&gt;</li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO\" title=\"2008 USAMO\">2008 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2008\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2008_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2008 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017122908\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.030 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 247/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1313/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7158/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.018      1 -total\n 52.31%    6.810      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 46.06%    5.996      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6860:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017122908 and revision id 128847. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}